---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Affiliate Disclosure — Formation.Legal"
  description="How Formation.Legal funds its independent research through transparent affiliate relationships."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <div class="mb-10 border-b border-[var(--color-border)] pb-8">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text-primary)] sm:text-4xl">Affiliate Disclosure</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Last updated: April 2026</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-lg">
      <p>
        Formation.Legal is an independent research platform. To keep our core research, datasets, and the Route Planner tool free for founders, we generate revenue through affiliate partnerships.
      </p>

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>
        When you click on links to various merchants or service providers on this site and make a purchase, this can result in this site earning a commission. This comes at absolutely <strong>no additional cost to you</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>Our Editorial Guarantee</h2>
      <p>
        Our affiliate relationships <strong>do not dictate our recommendations</strong>.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>We only recommend a provider if they legitimately fit a specific founder's "route" (business model, country, and banking needs).</li>
        <li>We routinely highlight the negative aspects, hidden fees, and limitations of providers that pay us commissions.</li>
        <li>If a non-commission provider is the best option for a specific route, we will recommend them over a commission-paying provider.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The Reality of Formation Affiliates</h2>
      <p>
        Many formation blogs exist solely to push the provider with the highest payout. We explicitly reject this model. Our value proposition is our accuracy regarding bank account approvals, compliance requirements, and Stripe access for non-US residents. Recommending the wrong provider for a quick commission would destroy that value.
      </p>

      <p>
        If you have questions about our affiliate links or how we fund our research, please contact us.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
